<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48668" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trādĭtor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		id (post-Aug.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A betrayer</i>, <i>traitor</i>, for
			the usual proditor: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">interfecto traditore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					4, 24</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sedul. Carm. 5, 61</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aug.
				Bapt. 7, 2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A teacher</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alicujus scientiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 3, 113</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tert. Coron. Mil. 4 <i>fin.</i></span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
